<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The right airing cupboard shelves turn a warm, cluttered cupboard into the best linen store in the house. Most British airing cupboards were built around a hot water cylinder, with a couple of wobbly shelves squeezed in above it, so towels end up in piles and the bedding you need is always at the bottom.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This guide shows what to store where, how to fit slatted shelves safely around a cylinder or boiler, and 16 airing cupboard storage ideas for towels, bedding sets, small cupboards and rented homes, plus the mistakes to avoid.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/airing-cupboard-01-hero.jpg" alt="Airing cupboard shelves: slatted pine shelves of folded white and sage towels and bedding above a white insulated hot water cylinder in an open landing cupboard" class="wp-image-2121" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/airing-cupboard-01-hero.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/airing-cupboard-01-hero-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/airing-cupboard-01-hero-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/airing-cupboard-01-hero-768x768.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group dsh-summary has-background" style="border-radius:12px;border-left-color:#8FA689;border-left-width:5px;background-color:#EEF3EC;padding-top:20px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:24px"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-0d2d72cd wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> The best airing cupboard shelves are slatted wooden shelves fixed on battens to the walls, starting above the hot water cylinder so the cylinder, pipes and valves stay easy to reach. Keep towels and bedding you use every week in the middle, spares on the top shelf, and never cover the slats or pack the cupboard so tightly that air cannot move.</li>



<li>Use the shelf just above the cylinder to finish off items that are only slightly damp, never soaking wet ones.</li>



<li>Keep paint, aerosols and cleaning products out of any cupboard with a gas boiler.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Time:</strong> an hour to reorganise, a morning to fit new shelves · <strong>Cost:</strong> £ to ££ · <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy to moderate</p>
</div></div>


