it">5. Use a Freestanding Slatted Unit</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#6-go-floor-to-ceiling-after-a-combi-swap">6. Go Floor to Ceiling After a Combi Swap</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#airing-cupboard-storage-ideas">Airing Cupboard Storage Ideas</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#7-store-bedding-sets-inside-a-pillowcase">7. Store Bedding Sets Inside a Pillowcase</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#8-give-each-shelf-one-job">8. Give Each Shelf One Job</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#9-roll-hand-towels-and-flannels">9. Roll Hand Towels and Flannels</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#10-keep-spare-duvets-in-cotton-bags">10. Keep Spare Duvets in Cotton Bags</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#11-use-the-back-of-the-door">11. Use the Back of the Door</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#12-sort-by-room-or-by-person">12. Sort by Room or by Person</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#airing-and-warmth-ideas">Airing and Warmth Ideas</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#13-finish-off-slightly-damp-items">13. Finish Off Slightly Damp Items</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#14-never-cover-the-slats">14. Never Cover the Slats</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#15-leave-room-for-air-to-move">15. Leave Room for Air to Move</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#16-insulate-the-cylinder">16. Insulate the Cylinder</a></li></ul></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#common-airing-cupboard-mistakes">Common Airing Cupboard Mistakes</a></li><li><a class="kb-table-of-contents__entry" href="#airing-cupboard-faq">Airing Cupboard FAQ</a><ul class="kb-table-of-contents-list-sub"><li><a cla